-- The Project Data Manager (Production V1 Wave 2, ADR-030).
--
-- One value on one enum, generated by drizzle-kit from the schema so the snapshot and the
-- migrations stay in agreement (the drift check in CI is what keeps them so). The role's
-- *permissions* are code — `PROJECT_ROLE_PERMISSIONS` in `@eia/domain` — because that is where
-- every other role's are, and a set living half in a table and half in TypeScript is a set nothing
-- keeps in agreement (the argument ADR-020 makes for the quality rule catalogue).
--
-- Additive and forward-only: `ADD VALUE` appends to the enum, no row changes, nothing is dropped,
-- and a database that has not run this simply has one fewer role a membership could name.
ALTER TYPE "app"."project_role" ADD VALUE 'PROJECT_DATA_MANAGER' BEFORE 'SOCIAL_SPECIALIST';
